WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.047
Euclid's Elements, Book One, Proposition Forty-Four.

2
00:00:04.047 --> 00:00:10.603
Apply to a given segment, in a given angle, a parallelogram equal in area to a given triangle.

3
00:00:10.603 --> 00:00:15.764
Let A B be the given segment, C the given triangle, and D the given angle.

4
00:00:15.764 --> 00:00:22.250
We apply to segment A B, in an angle equal to D, a parallelogram equal in area to triangle C.

5
00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:33.399
By Proposition Forty-Two, construct parallelogram B E F G equal in area to triangle C in angle E B G equal to angle D, placed so that B E is in a line with A B.

6
00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:38.697
Extend F G to H, draw A H through A parallel to B G, and construct segment H B.

7
00:00:38.697 --> 00:00:46.140
Because transversal H F falls on parallels A H and E F, interior angles A H F and H F E equal two right angles.

8
00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:54.053
Thus angles B H G and G F E are less than two right angles, so by the Fifth Postulate, H B and F E extended will meet.

9
00:00:54.053 --> 00:01:00.960
Extend them to meet at K, draw K L through K parallel to E A, and extend H A and G B to points L and M.

10
00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:11.924
Now H L K F is a parallelogram with diameter H K, having parallelograms H A B G and B M K E about H K, and complements A B M L and B E F G.

11
00:01:11.924 --> 00:01:23.530
By Proposition Forty-Three, complement A B M L equals complement B E F G, which was constructed equal to triangle C; therefore A B M L equals triangle C.

12
00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:33.164
Moreover, by Proposition Fifteen, vertical angle A B M equals angle E B G, which equals angle D; so angle A B M equals angle D.

13
00:01:33.164 --> 00:01:43.860
Therefore parallelogram A B M L, equal to triangle C, has been applied to segment A B in angle A B M equal to angle D, as was required to do.
